0:{"buildId":"7afh9cBoHBO9HIwX4Lcyt","data":[{"rsc":["$","$1","c",{"children":[["$","$L2",null,{"toc":[{"depth":2,"url":"#two-axes-and-only-one-of-them-is-a-forge-knob","title":"Two axes, and only one of them is a Forge knob"},{"depth":2,"url":"#sizing-one-worker","title":"Sizing one worker"},{"depth":2,"url":"#the-ceilings-you-hit-before-you-expect-to","title":"The ceilings you hit before you expect to"},{"depth":2,"url":"#the-signal-to-scale-on","title":"The signal to scale on"},{"depth":2,"url":"#scaling-out","title":"Scaling out"},{"depth":2,"url":"#what-the-repository-actually-ships","title":"What the repository actually ships"},{"depth":2,"url":"#backpressure-when-a-worker-needs-to-stop","title":"Backpressure, when a worker needs to stop"},{"depth":2,"url":"#heterogeneous-pools","title":"Heterogeneous pools"},{"depth":2,"url":"#when-it-doesnt-work","title":"When it doesn't work"}],"children":[["$","$L3",null,{"children":"Scaling workers"}],["$","$L4",null,{"children":"How much work one worker should take, how many workers you need, which signal tells you, and how to let something else make the decision, including the parts Forge does not enforce for you."}],["$","$L5",null,{"children":["\n",["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Who this is for:"}]," you have a worker pool serving real builds and the queue is\neither backing up or sitting idle. ",["$","strong",null,{"children":"What you'll have at the end:"}]," a sized\nworker, a scaling signal you trust, and either a manual playbook or an\nautoscaler wired to it. ",["$","strong",null,{"children":"Time:"}]," an afternoon for the manual version, longer if\nyou're building the autoscaling path."]}],"\n",["$","div",null,{"data-prerequisites":true,"className":"my-6 rounded-xl border border-border bg-surface-elevated px-5 py-3","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"my-0 font-mono text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-brand","children":"Before you start"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"mt-1 text-sm text-muted-foreground [&>p]:my-0","children":["$","p",null,{"children":"A worker pool serving real builds."}]}]]}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","$L6",null,{"href":"/how-to/run-multiple-workers","children":"Run multiple workers"}]," is how you get from one\nworker to several. This page is about the questions that come next: how much\nwork each one should take, how many you need, and who decides."]}],"\n",["$","$L7",null,{"as":"h2","id":"two-axes-and-only-one-of-them-is-a-forge-knob","children":"Two axes, and only one of them is a Forge knob"}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":"Capacity has a vertical axis (how many actions one worker runs at once) and a\nhorizontal axis (how many workers exist). Forge has a field for the first.\nIt has nothing at all for the second, by design: a worker is a process that\ndials the scheduler and announces itself, so \"more workers\" means \"start more\nprocesses,\" and whatever starts processes for you is the thing that scales."}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":"Start with the vertical axis, because it changes what the horizontal one costs."}],"\n",["$","$L7",null,{"as":"h2","id":"sizing-one-worker","children":"Sizing one worker"}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":["The knob is ",["$","code",null,{"children":"max_inflight_tasks"}]," on the worker's config."]}],"\n",["$","$L8",null,{"className":"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark","style":{"--shiki-light":"#24292e","--shiki-dark":"#e1e4e8","--shiki-light-bg":"#fff","--shiki-dark-bg":"#24292e"},"tabIndex":"0","icon":"<svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M 6,1 C 4.354992,1 3,2.354992 3,4 v 16 c 0,1.645008 1.354992,3 3,3 h 12 c 1.645008,0 3,-1.354992 3,-3 V 8 7 A 1.0001,1.0001 0 0 0 20.707031,6.2929687 l -5,-5 A 1.0001,1.0001 0 0 0 15,1 h -1 z m 0,2 h 7 v 3 c 0,1.645008 1.354992,3 3,3 h 3 v 11 c 0,0.564129 -0.435871,1 -1,1 H 6 C 5.4358712,21 5,20.564129 5,20 V 4 C 5,3.4358712 5.4358712,3 6,3 Z M 15,3.4140625 18.585937,7 H 16 C 15.435871,7 15,6.5641288 15,6 Z\" fill=\"currentColor\" /></svg>","children":"$L9"}],"\n","$La","\n","$Lb","\n","$Lc","\n","$Ld","\n","$Le","\n","$Lf","\n","$L10","\n","$L11","\n","$L12","\n","$L13","\n","$L14","\n","$L15","\n","$L16","\n","$L17","\n","$L18","\n","$L19","\n","$L1a","\n","$L1b","\n","$L1c","\n","$L1d","\n","$L1e","\n","$L1f","\n","$L20","\n","$L21","\n","$L22","\n","$L23","\n","$L24","\n","$L25","\n","$L26","\n","$L27","\n","$L28","\n","$L29","\n","$L2a","\n","$L2b","\n","$L2c","\n","$L2d","\n","$L2e","\n","$L2f","\n","$L30","\n","$L31","\n","$L32","\n","$L33","\n","$L34","\n","$L35","\n","$L36","\n","$L37","\n","$L38","\n","$L39","\n","$L3a"]}],"$L3b"]}],["$L3c","$L3d"],"$L3e"]}],"isPartial":"$@3f","staleTime":"$40","varyParams":null},{"rsc":"$L41","isPartial":"$@42","staleTime":"$40","varyParams":null},{"rsc":"$L43","isPartial":"$@44","staleTime":"$40","varyParams":"$45"}],"isUpgradeableISRFallback":false,"a":"$@46","rootVaryParams":null,"needsRuntimeRequest":"$@47"}
